        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2fcf572c-aef6-502a-b3da-ada46b311363",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm\n- Places: Liverpool Bay, Irish Sea, Wales, northeast Wales, Cheshire, Lancashire, Merseyside\n- Vessels: SS Ellan Vannin\n- Topics: Offshore wind power, maritime loss\n\nFacts:\n- Liverpool Bay is a bay of the Irish Sea located between northeast Wales and the English counties of Cheshire, Lancashire, and Merseyside.\n- SS Ellan Vannin served under the name \"Ellan Vannin\" for a further 26 years before being lost in a storm in Liverpool Bay on 3 December 1909.\n- North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm is Wales's first offshore wind farm and the United Kingdom's first major offshore renewable power project.",
